cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "itj: a jet toy for learning representations and interpretability of jet taggers"
abstract: >-
  A jet toy simulated from first principles ("A Spray of Hadrons"): QCD, W and top jets from a hard process, a
  coherent parton shower, hadronisation, the underlying event and a simple detector, written with the branches of
  the JetClass data set and a full truth record; tools that run the same analysis on the toy and on JetClass
  (clustering, substructure observables, network inputs identical to weaver, ParticleNet and the Particle
  Transformer with pretrained JetClass weights, probes, attributions and self-supervised learning) and student
  tasks on representation learning and interpretability of jet taggers.
